From 2b116b426dd5af86be897791b3a30e3a8365a183 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:20:26 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 03/22] fix(reframe): only delegate a reactor clip when its
 inset is measurable

A two-pane video-call podcast has a small, still face in an upper corner
and another face lower down, so find_reactor_face fired and the EDL
planner delegated the clip to the plain path. The plain path could not
measure a facecam rectangle either and fell back to a small-faces fit.
With the source path, build_reframe_plan now asks for the same two-part
evidence as choose_reaction_layout (face + measurable inset), sampled
inside the clip's ranges. Callers without a source path keep the old
face-only check; REFRAME_REACTOR_NEEDS_INSET=0 restores it everywhere.

Proof: podcast 1oXjtK5Nsjw clip 2 now renders as split (both faces
large) instead of fit; the facecam fixture still delegates.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
